Below is a one-line change to the VB grammar so that an apostrophe or REM-style comment will “swallow” any immediately following continuation lines (those ending in `_`).  We simply make the comment rule multiline (greedy) and look for any `\r\n`+whitespace+underscore sequence:

```javascript
### components/prism-visual-basic.js
