=======
    'comment': {
        // Match a comment plus any VB line-continuations (_) on the next lines
        pattern: /(?:['‘’]|REM\b)[^\r\n]*(?:\r\n[ \t]*_[^\r\n]*)*/i,
        inside: {
            'keyword': /^REM/i
        },
        greedy: true
    },
>>>>>>> REPLACE
```

Explanation of the change:

- We replace the old single-line comment regex `/(?:['‘’]|REM\b).*/i` with a new one that:
  1. Starts the same (`(?:['‘’]|REM\b)`).
  2. Consumes everything up to the first newline (`[^\r\n]*`).
  3. Optionally repeats any “line-continuation” segments: a CRLF plus optional tabs/spaces then an underscore, then the rest of that line (`(?:\r\n[ \t]*_[^\r\n]*)*`).
- We also add `greedy: true` so that Prism will consume all of it as a single comment token.
- As soon as a comment line does **not** end in `_`, the rule will stop and highlighting will resume normally. This now correctly highlights continuations of commented lines as comments.

